{:edb/db-before-t 2151 :edb/db-after-t 2152 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535464 50 #inst "2026-10-09T00:38:50.225Z" 13194139535464 true] [17592186105657 1020 #edb/ref 17592186350582 13194139535464 true] [17592186105657 1020 #edb/ref 17592186350585 13194139535464 true] [17592186105658 1020 #edb/ref 17592186350575 13194139535464 true] [17592186105658 1020 #edb/ref 17592186350592 13194139535464 true] [17592186350575 1017 #edb/ref 17592186350576 13194139535464 true] [17592186350575 1089 "q-128008" 13194139535464 true] [17592186350575 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535464 true] [17592186350575 1100 "Calculate the length of the altitude $RH$ of the $△\\,PRQ,$ if $P(3,0,4),$ $Q(2,3,1),$ $R(0,3,1).$" 13194139535464 true] [17592186350575 1113 #uuid "0a2fce35-3849-53f0-9cee-8dbfca3f9123" 13194139535464 true] [17592186350575 1145 "Note that the length of the altitude $RH$ can be related to the area of $△\\,PQR$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}RH\\cdot PQ\n$$\n\nSo, to find $RH,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =(2i+3j+k)-(3i+4k) \\\\  & =-i+3j-3j \\\\  & =⟨-1,3,-3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =(3j+k)-(3i+4k) \\\\  & =-3i+3j-3k \\\\  & =⟨-3,3,-3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 3 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ -3 & -3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3\\cdot (-3)-3\\cdot (-3))i-((-1)\\cdot (-3)-(-3)\\cdot (-3))j+((-1)\\cdot 3-(-3)\\cdot 3)k \\\\  & =6j+6k \\\\  & =⟨0,6,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{PR}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{6}^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{72} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,PQR$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{6\\sqrt{2}}{2}=3\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $PQ$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}PQ & =|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{19}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}RH\\cdot PQ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}RH\\cdot PQ \\\\ 3\\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}RH\\cdot \\sqrt{19} \\\\ 6\\sqrt{2} & =RH\\cdot \\sqrt{19} \\\\ RH & =\\frac{6\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{19}} \\\\ RH & =\\frac{6\\sqrt{38}}{19}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535464 true] [17592186350576 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350577 13194139535464 true] [17592186350576 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350578 13194139535464 true] [17592186350576 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350579 13194139535464 true] [17592186350576 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350580 13194139535464 true] [17592186350576 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350581 13194139535464 true] [17592186350576 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535464 true] [17592186350576 1041 "selection" 13194139535464 true] [17592186350576 1104 #edb/ref 17592186350577 13194139535464 true] [17592186350576 1110 #uuid "6d873505-a18c-5dbd-b872-957b944e5ae6" 13194139535464 true] [17592186350577 1034 "\\frac{6\\sqrt{38}}{19}" 13194139535464 true] [17592186350577 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535464 true] [17592186350577 1111 #uuid "f99fa164-3ecd-58bc-bb9b-7d8bd15a74d7" 13194139535464 true] [17592186350578 1034 "\\frac{3\\sqrt{38}}{19}" 13194139535464 true] [17592186350578 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535464 true] [17592186350578 1111 #uuid "c68f18a2-3893-5427-b42d-b8f9d6de0c84" 13194139535464 true] [17592186350579 1034 "2" 13194139535464 true] [17592186350579 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535464 true] [17592186350579 1111 #uuid "e411